---
name: dev-fix
version: 1.1.0
description: lead dev-fix assignment for a dev bead reopened after a failed sanity check. Same bead (task_id), same branch; its open child finding beads are the work.
format: xml
required_variables:
  - task_id
  - sprint
  - stack
  - worktree_path
  - branch
  - pr_target
  - primary_checkout
  - phase_root
  - lead
  - cc
  - test_command
optional_variables:
  - sanity_bead
defaults:
  sanity_bead: ""
metadata:
  type: dev-fix
  tags:
    - stage:dev
    - orchestration:beads
  workflow:
    scope:
      kind: sprint
      variable: sprint
    state: dev-start
    stage: dev
    transition: start
---
<atm-task id="{{ task_id }}" sprint="{{ sprint }}" mode="dev-fix">
  <description><![CDATA[{% if sanity_bead %}Sanity check `{{ sanity_bead | string | cdata_escape }}` failed dev bead `{{ task_id | string | cdata_escape }}` and {{ lead | string | cdata_escape }} reopened it.{% else %}{{ lead | string | cdata_escape }} reopened dev bead `{{ task_id | string | cdata_escape }}` after plan review.{% endif %} Its open child finding beads are the work. `bd show {{ task_id | string | cdata_escape }}` is still the assignment.]]></description>

  <worktree><![CDATA[{{ worktree_path | string | cdata_escape }}]]></worktree>
  <branch><![CDATA[{{ branch | string | cdata_escape }}]]></branch>
  <stack><![CDATA[{{ stack | string | cdata_escape }}]]></stack>
  <stack-discipline><![CDATA[`{{ branch | string | cdata_escape }}` is not linked. Commit the fixes there and rebase only onto `origin/{{ pr_target | string | cdata_escape }}`. Never edit another branch and never run `gh stack link`, `sync`, `rebase` or `merge`.]]></stack-discipline>

  <workflow>
    <step id="a"><![CDATA[Before claiming, run `git fetch origin && git rebase origin/{{ pr_target | string | cdata_escape }}` in the worktree (a conflict is part of the fix), then `{{ primary_checkout | string | cdata_escape }}/.claude/skills/atm-bd-orchestration/scripts/assignment-gates.py dev --root {{ phase_root | string | cdata_escape }} --bead {{ task_id | string | cdata_escape }} --pr-target {{ pr_target | string | cdata_escape }} --worktree {{ worktree_path | string | cdata_escape }}` from the worktree (scripts come from the primary checkout, never the branch). Each check, its command and its refusal code: (1) plan valid: `{{ primary_checkout | string | cdata_escape }}/.claude/skills/atm-beads/scripts/validate-plan --root {{ phase_root | string | cdata_escape }}` exits 0, else `PLAN_INVALID`; (2) ready: `bd ready -n 0 --json` lists the bead, else `NOT_READY`; (3) claimable without `--force`: `bd show {{ task_id | string | cdata_escape }} --json` shows status `open` and assignee empty or `$ATM_IDENTITY`, else `UNCLAIMABLE`; (4) target: `metadata.pr_target` equals `{{ pr_target | string | cdata_escape }}`, else `PR_TARGET_MISMATCH`; (5) difficulty: your `atm members --json` model is in `DIFFICULTY_MODELS[metadata.difficulty]`, else `DIFFICULTY_MISMATCH`; (6) base: `git merge-base --is-ancestor origin/{{ pr_target | string | cdata_escape }} HEAD` exits 0, else `WRONG_BASE`. `GATE_CANNOT_RUN` when a command fails. Reuse an existing workflow class bead for the same failure signature: append the task id, head, command and failure evidence, and cite the class id in the refusal. If no class matches, report the signature to {{ lead | string | cdata_escape }} for classification and cite that message instead; do not create a per-task shadow or delay the refusal. A successful check permits a normal claim and task start.]]></step>
    <step id="a1"><![CDATA[When it prints `false` the bead is not ready: do not claim it and do not start the task. Find the root cause: `bd show {{ task_id | string | cdata_escape }}` (status, assignee; still `closed` means it was never reopened), `bd blocked --json | jq --arg b {{ task_id | string | cdata_escape }} '.[] | select(.id == $b)'` (its open blockers), and `bd show <blocker>` for each. Report it with `atm send {{ lead | string | cdata_escape }} --stdin`: the bead, why it is not ready, and which bead or agent has to move. Then wait.]]></step>
    <step id="b"><![CDATA[Read `bd show {{ task_id | string | cdata_escape }}` and its open child beads (`bd list --parent {{ task_id | string | cdata_escape }} --status open --json`). Fix each one and close it individually: `bd close <child> --reason "<short sha>: <what fixed it>"`. Then re-check the whole bead: the sanity check reports what it saw, not everything that is missing. Do not weaken a test or criterion to make a finding go away. The bead's `metadata.requirements` and `metadata.adrs` still govern the fix: re-read each one it names.]]></step>
    <step id="c"><![CDATA[Run `{{ test_command | string | cdata_escape }}` and the bead's validation commands until they pass with zero failures.]]></step>
    <step id="d"><![CDATA[Rebase only onto `origin/{{ pr_target | string | cdata_escape }}` (`git fetch origin && git rebase origin/{{ pr_target | string | cdata_escape }}`), re-run `{{ test_command | string | cdata_escape }}`, then `git push --force-with-lease origin {{ branch | string | cdata_escape }}`.]]></step>
    <step id="e"><![CDATA[Close the bead and the task together: `bd close {{ task_id | string | cdata_escape }} --reason "dev complete at <short sha>"` and `atm task close {{ task_id | string | cdata_escape }} completed --template .claude/skills/atm-bd-orchestration/templates/dev-complete.md.j2 --vars <scratch>/dev-complete-{{ task_id | string | cdata_escape }}-vars.json`. In the vars, `deliverables_md` lists each finding and what fixed it. The sanity check then runs again on the new head. Only this close frees your queue.{% if cc and cc != lead %} Copy a one-line summary to `{{ cc | string | cdata_escape }}` with a plain `atm send {{ cc | string | cdata_escape }} --stdin`.{% endif %}]]></step>
    <step id="e1"><![CDATA[If the bead cannot be completed at all, reuse an existing workflow class bead for the same failure signature: append the task id, head, command and failure evidence, and cite the class id in the refusal. If no class matches, report the signature to {{ lead | string | cdata_escape }} for classification and cite that message instead; do not create a per-task shadow or delay the refusal. Declare failure with `bd update {{ task_id | string | cdata_escape }} --status blocked --assignee "" --append-notes "DEV_CANNOT_COMPLETE; workflow class or escalation <reference>: <reason>"` (never `bd close`: a closed dev bead releases its sanity check) and `atm task close {{ task_id | string | cdata_escape }} refused --template .claude/skills/atm-bd-orchestration/templates/task-refused.md.j2 --vars <scratch>/refused-{{ task_id | string | cdata_escape }}-vars.json`.]]></step>
    <step id="f"><![CDATA[After the close, read ATM again: the next queued task starts only now.]]></step>
  </workflow>
</atm-task>
